<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20861" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὅμηρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Greek poet
			Homer</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 1, 1, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 32,
			79</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 2, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Brut.
				10, 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Arch. 8, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de
				Or. 3, 34, 137</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1, 5, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint.
				10, 1, 47 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P. 359
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηρικός</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Homer</i>, <i>Homeric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 25, 52</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dispositio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 12, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facultas eloquendi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 1, 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">more,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					7, 10, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ajax,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 39, 82</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Agamemno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 3, 26, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Nestor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 4, 3, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi,</span>”
				i. e. <i>blind</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 2</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērĭă-cus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">notae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Priap. 69</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scyphi, quos Homerios a caelatura carminum
					Homeri vocabat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 47</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērista</span></b> ,
				ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηριστής</span>, <i>a Homeric
			rhapsodist</i>, <i><span class="en">Petr. 29</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Diom. p. 481</span></i>
			P.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērŏnĭdes</span></b> ,
				ae, m., <i>an imitator of
				Homer</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 2, 6, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
